    <!--
      R49, ticket 67 - mob 8300007 "Dragon Rider": the rows STAY, and there are SEVENTEEN of them.

      Two of our own changeSets looked like they contradicted each other.
      153-crimson-sky-drop-data.sql:39-40 refused to table 8300007: "no map IN SCOPE places it and
      no v84 mob-skill summon list names it, so nothing can kill it. Add one when a spawner
      exists." That refusal was scoped to the Crimson Sky work, not a general prohibition, so
      160-monsterbook-drop-data.sql:271-287 tabling it later is compatible with it and is the
      later, more specific statement. 153 is APPLIED and is NOT edited; this note is the
      annotation. No row was added or removed by ticket 67.

      All seventeen rows at 160-monsterbook-drop-data.sql:271-287 are covered by this decision, not
      just the six weapon tablets at :282-287 that R49 was written about:
        :271     2000005
        :272-276 2049100, 2049201, 2049203, 2049205, 2049207
        :277-281 2040502, 2040505, 2040514, 2040517, 2040534
        :282-287 2047000, 2047001, 2047002, 2047100, 2047101, 2047102

      They are not derived. String.wz/MonsterBook.img/8300007/reward lists exactly those seventeen
      item ids in exactly that order - the client's own per-mob drop list, which is what all of
      changeSet 160 transcribes and what MonsterBookDropV84RealLoad re-derives row by row.

      The mob is still placed by nothing: no file under wz/Map.wz/ names 8300007, so every one of
      the seventeen rows is inert until a spawner exists. Inert is not wrong - removing a working
      table to satisfy a scoped aside would lose it for whenever a spawner does appear. The
      MonsterBook entry's own map/0=240080800 is a client display hint, not a server spawn.

      The ten ACCESSORY tablets 2047300-2047309 get NO row. No mob's MonsterBook reward list names
      any of them anywhere in v84, so there is nothing to transcribe, and their only analogue is
      the six weapon tablets above - copying those would propagate the same unplaced dropper and
      manufacture the appearance of a source. The fix for them is a spawner, not a drop row.
      MonsterBookDropV84RealLoad.dragonRiderRowsStayAndAccessoryTabletsGetNone pins both halves.
    -->
